    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §8-600, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5101\n\nSPONSOR: GONZALEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to early voting for\ncertain special elections; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nModifies the hours of early voting for any special elections held on\nApril 29, 2025, to account for religious holidays.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Provides that early voting for any special election held on\nApril 29, 2025, shall begin on April 21, 2025 and shall end on April 27,\n2025.\n\nSection 2. Provides that the duration of early voting hours for any\nspecial election held on April 29, 2025, shall be equal to or greater\nthan the minimum number of total hours otherwise required by law.\n\nSection 3. Effective Date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMillions of New York City residents observe Passover and Easter holi-\ndays, which coincide with the slated early voting period for the April\n29 special election. To accommodate these holidays, this bill proposes\nto modify the early voting period for this election to run from April 21\nto April 27 with the requirement that the total number of available\nhours for early voting remain the same as otherwise required by law.\nSimilar adjustments were made to the early voting period for the 2024\nPresidential Primary to account for the Easter holiday.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENT:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that sections\none and two of this act shall expire December 31, 2025 when upon such\ndate the provisions of this act shall be deemed repealed.\n",
